 one patch-agent session complete more than one reviewed patch without a later hash replacing earlier
 reviewed work in the linearizer prompt.
 
+After a review completes for a patch agent, the controller appends the review result to that
+patch-agent chat, appends `work-leaf: is this feature done? yes/no`, and selects the patch-agent
+session. Terminal adapters track that prompt as a close-confirmation state: `yes` hides the
+patch-agent row from the left pane, `no` keeps the chat available and clears the ready marker, and any
+other response is sent as normal chat after the close-confirmation state is cleared.
+
 The command transcript is also the conversation history for the persistent `command-agent`. That
 system agent interprets chat sent to the Work Leaf command surface. It recognizes literal command
 lines and common natural-language requests for help, review, linearization, quitting, and launching
